+## Detect test failures with GitHub Actions
+
+The [GitHub Action](/docs/get-started/ci) runs your Doc Detective tests on every push or pull request. When a test fails, the action can surface the failure in your repository so that you and your AI integrations can act on it.
+
+To detect failures and hand them off to integrations, set `create_issue_on_fail` and `integrations` in your workflow:
+
+```yaml
+name: doc-detective
+on: [pull_request]
+
+jobs:
+  runTests:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    permissions:
+      contents: read
+      issues: write
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: doc-detective/github-action@v1
+        with:
+          create_issue_on_fail: true
+          integrations: claude
+```
+
+When tests fail, the action creates a GitHub issue that includes the test results and mentions the configured integrations. The issue body can include the test results (`$RESULTS`), the workflow run URL (`$RUN_URL`), and the prompt text (`$PROMPT`). For the full list of issue options, see [Create issues on test failure](/docs/get-started/ci#create-issues-on-test-failure).
+
+## Get AI analysis of potential fixes
+
+After the issue is created, each configured integration analyzes the failure and responds with an explanation of likely causes and suggested fixes. The analysis appears as a comment on the issue, so you can review the suggestions, apply fixes, and re-run the workflow.
+
+- **Claude, Cursor, Dosu, Doc Sentinel, and OpenCode** are mentioned in the issue and respond with analysis and suggestions.
+- **Copilot** is assigned to the issue and responds through GitHub Copilot.
+- **Promptless** analyzes failures and can automatically create documentation updates.
+
